new Assassin's Creed details have leaked  plus The Last of Us Part 1 and Nintendo  switch sports are getting new features  so in yesterday's Gamespot news I  mentioned how the future of Assassin's  Creed would be revealed during an event  in September well it seems the franchise  couldn't wait because details have  surfaced about two games codenamed  project red and project Rift Kotaku  reported on Project Red's existence  while Bloomberg's Jason schreier said  project red is a part of AC Infinity as  opposed to a separate Game Source is  speaking to Kotaku said this game  whatever it may be could be set in Asia  reporter Jeff Grubb of sister site Giant  Bomb previously said it may be said in  Japan kotaku's own sources could not  confirm this but the site's insiders  said Japan as a setting for Assassin's  Creed has long been discussed internally  and that's no surprise as Ubisoft has  spoken openly over the years about how  Japan has been considered as a setting  for a future Assassin's Creed game but  project red and infinity aren't the only  new Assassin's Creed games in the works  at Ubisoft right now during an earnings  report call the company mentioned a  delay for another smaller premium  unannounced title reports now indicate  the game in question is Project Rift a  standalone AC game that was originally  meant to be DLC for Assassin's Creed  Valhalla according to Bloomberg News  Ubisoft bordeaux's office which is  leading development on the project  requested the game be pushed from its  targeted February launch due to the game  running far behind schedule the game is  now slated for release in May or June  according to the report which will move  it from ubisoft's 2023 fiscal calendar  now moving on to another game with  stealth elements The Last of Us Part One  naughty dog has revealed more details on  how the game has been remade for PS5 and  PC in a new deep dive video while the  core gameplay is essentially the same  players can expect graphical upgrades  new features and enhancements that make  the game more accessible some of the new  features outlined in the Playstation  blog post include a new permadeath mode  a speed run mode an updated photo mode  mode unlockable costumes for Joel and  Ellie and a model viewer mode on the  technical side The Last of Us Part 1 can  render in Native 4K at a targeted 30 FPS  or a dynamic 4K at a targeted 60 FPS  display mode the added power of the PS5  means that environments have denser  physics with tons of bumpables and  chipables that translate into gunfire  ripping concrete and other objects apart  more accurately with more than 60  accessibility options players can also  expect an audio description mode that  makes the title more easily playable The  Last of Us Part One will launch for PS5  on September 2nd but a PC release date  has yet to be announced now let's talk  about a game that will never come to PS5  or PC Nintendo switch Sports Nintendo  has announced that it will be adding  full motion control support for soccer  in switch Sports on July 26th this free  update is scheduled to go live at 6 PM  Pacific 9 pm Eastern and will include a  number of new features including the  ability for players to use the motion of  their legs to kick the soccer ball in  game when using the leg strap accessory  players will also be able to use their  hands while jogging in place to in-game  dash Nintendo explained that playing  this wave will translate users in-game  kicks to be more powerful and the update  doesn't just address leg strap players  it will also allow new moves in  volleyball such as Slide Attack and  Rocket serve aside from the motion  control support feature the game is also  adding new s-rank and infinity rank in  online pro league mode meanwhile I'm  over here just patiently waiting for the  promise golf mode to arrive and praying  hoping that it's followed up by a  surprise announcement of baseball making  its return  but until then I guess this update is  cool too let me know what sports you  want to make its way into Nintendo  switch Sports have a great weekend and  Tom we'll see you next week
 

